The mapping behavior appears preserved, but the new stmap78 diagnostic can emit incorrect path phase information for inverter-fallback reconstruction paths, which undermines the feature being added.

Review comment:

- [P2] Fix demand-path phases for inverter fallback — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/base/abci/abcMap.c:947-947
  When a node has no best cut for the requested phase, this push records `fPhase` on the demand-path stack but the code later recurses through `Abc_NodeFromMapPhase_rec(..., !fPhase)`. For watched leaves reached through that inverter fallback, `demand-path` rows report the parent/path phase from the outer request rather than the cut phase that actually requested the leaf, so the lineage diagnostic can contradict `demand-leaf` and misidentify downstream request phases.
